		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: HELP!!! MD-9600 programming]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4243&amp;p=32123#p32123"><![CDATA[
CPS:<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/" class="postlink">downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/</a><br><br>Firmware (If you got it recently) i'd suggest to try a HW V5 firmware.<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD9600/Firmware/0c885b34e52cca7e946d82a4881bb211cb488e61/" class="postlink">downloads/MD9600/Firmware/0c885b34e52cc ... 1cb488e61/</a><br><br><br>Donor file:<br>I used this donor file<br><a href="https://www.passion-radio.com/index.php?controller=attachment&amp;id_attachment=760" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.com/index.php ... chment=760</a><br><br>Unzip the donor firmware zip file, to extract the donor file MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin<br>Note. This file is the same for all MD9600 hardware versions.<br><br>I wrote a bit about converting mine here.<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=18&amp;t=4211#p32001" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=18&amp;t=4211#p32001</a><br><br><br>.<br><br>Re: Comport ...<br>The MD-9600 will NOT show up as a serial-device (ComPort) , until you have loaded the OpenGD77 firmware into the device, and it has rebooted..<br><br>With "Factory firmware" it will "only" show up as a USB "STM device in DFU mode" i the windows hw manager<br><br>.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5917">OZ1FTG</a> — Sun Jul 14, 2024 6:31 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
